  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Not exactly reproduction steps, however, these are the exact actions I did for the bug to occur, it occurs regardless of avatar, but it happened this time in my Charcoal Protogen avatar if you want to attempt to recreate it better.\n\n1. Open VRChat (VR or PC)\n\n2. Go into a world other than your home world with at least another individual.\n\n3. Jump, then enter the VRChat menu and click \"Go home\" (return to home)\n\n4. Tab out of VRChat onto an application, and type.\n\n5. Bug occurs.\n\nHOWEVER!\n\nI has happened to me on about six different occasions (over the course of about 3500 hours of gameplay, so, good luck), in VR, and in different avatars, its when you go to your home world on rare occasions, something about the IK and your \"pill\" rotates violently.\n\nI also happened to have an instance of the Unity Editor open this time, again, no clue on the requirements but I've had it happen in VR in different home-worlds and with different avatars and it is slightly nauseating. I was also switching server regions when doing this time, too. Vanilla client, for clarity, I know some fools report bugs when they are breaking TOS.\n\nLuckily I had the mirror open so if you're the dev good with the default VRChat IK controller and logistics you can get an in-depth look. Here's a link to the uncompressed video if you need any more detail for whatever reason:\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/337672341041446912/1098867268110274670/i_have_no_words.mp4\n\nMost likely doesn't matter but I was in \"A LONG DREAM\" during this occasion, no seats that could cause this, just a simple world and a post-processing layer.\n\nIt is completely random and unpredictable the only consistency is that it happens when going to your homeworld. I only managed to capture it because I happened to have been on desktop and OBS studio was fast to launch and already set to recording VRChat.",
